+Vice City VR is an unofficial standalone VR adaptation of the original 2003
+PC game, built on the reverse-engineered reVC codebase and the librw
+RenderWare-compatible renderer. This branch runs natively on Meta Quest through
+OpenXR and Vulkan; a gaming PC, Quest Link, Air Link, and SteamVR are not
+required while playing.
+
+The project is a work-in-progress alpha. The complete campaign has not yet
+been validated on the public Quest configuration.
+
+## Original game requirement
+
+This repository and its release packages do not include *Grand Theft Auto:
+Vice City* or any original game data. Each player must provide a legally
+obtained copy of the original 2003 PC release and copy the required data to the
+headset with the included installer.
+
+## Current native Quest features
+
+- Native OpenXR and Vulkan rendering for standalone Meta Quest.
+- Stereoscopic 6DOF gameplay with single-pass multiview world rendering.
+- Tracked VR hands, per-hand calibration, physical weapon handling, dual
+  wielding, and two-handed grips.
+- Motion-controlled firearms, melee combat, throwables, physical scopes, and a
+  usable mission camera.
+- Six configurable body holsters and optional manual reload interactions for
+  supported one-handed guns.
+- Default, immersive, and motion vehicle controls, including calibrated car
+  and motorcycle interactions.
+- One consistent vehicle-fire button: **B** fires in Default, Immersive, and
+  Motion driving modes, while the triggers remain available for throttle and
+  brake input.
+- In-headset VR settings, calibration, loadout, cheat, HUD, and diagnostic
+  menus.
+- Theater presentation for startup screens, frontend menus, and cutscenes.
+- Head-relative locomotion, smooth and snap turning, adjustable HUD layout,
+  and VR-specific mission controls.
+- Restored circular minimap, Vice City colour filtering, lighting, weather,
+  rain, water, transparency, and world effects.
+- Quest-focused streaming, draw preparation, Vulkan state caching, and
+  multiview optimisations, plus lightweight FXAA.
+- Save/load support for native Quest saves and converted saves from the current
+  Win64 Vice City VR build.
+
+## Install a release build
+
+The public release archive includes Windows and Linux/Steam Deck installers.
+They copy the required data from the player's legal PC installation and apply
+the small redistributable VR asset overlay.
+
+See [release/sidequest/INSTALL.md](release/sidequest/INSTALL.md) for complete
+player instructions. The Android package and data directory are:
+
